  "prefLabel": "Pdab 202.11 Consolidation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pdab 202.11 Consolidation. Upon motion or the board’s own initiative, if 2 or more proceedings involve common questions of law or fact, and the board determines consolidation is fair and efficient, the board shall consolidate those proceedings for hearing, decision, or both, after providing the parties notice and an opportunity for hearing on the proposed consolidation.\n\nSource. #13500-A, eff 12-2-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pdab100-300.html"
